{
  "description": "Deterministic keyword -> category/tag rules for Phase 2 retrieval (retrieval.js). Kept small and hand-readable on purpose (Phase 2 spec section 7: 'the retrieval process must be understandable and debuggable'). Matching is a case-insensitive substring test against the raw user prompt. No niche-specific words (e.g. 'pet', 'fashion') are included here deliberately — this taxonomy is generic e-commerce capability language, not niche/brand personalization, which belongs to a later phase (WebsiteBrief). See PHASE2_REPORT.md for how each rule was chosen and measured.",

  "defaultRule": {
    "description": "Fires for generic commercial-intent language that shows up in nearly every merchant request, regardless of niche. Establishes a sensible baseline set of homepage-relevant categories (mirrors the existing system prompt's own default-to-'modern'-palette philosophy in detectNicheAndGetColors()) rather than requiring every prompt to name specific capabilities by name.",
    "keywords": ["store", "shop", "website", "site", "brand", "page", "homepage", "business", "landing"],
    "categories": ["hero", "product-showcase", "social-proof", "conversion", "content"],
    "tags": []
  },

